		"meta": {
			"author": "Stefan Mazur",
			"category": "effect",
			"deploymentTarget": {
				"branch": "",
				"name": "Wire",
				"version": {
					"major": 7,
					"minor": 27,
					"patch": 0
				}
			},
			"description": "Autumn Wind - an effect: 16 kinds of items drift across the clip below with depth, gusts, tumble and eddies. Nothing moves by itself: drive Clock from Arena (Timeline, BPM Sync or FFT). If the clock stops, everything stops. Scale sizes everything relative to the output height; wide surfaces get items across the whole width. Physics: Wind and Fall as strength + direction (0 = right, 90 = up), Gust Sway, Tumble, Speed Variation, Eddies (how often and how strongly eddies whirl the items, 0 = off), Eddy Size. Every kind has its own weight: chestnuts drop, feathers drift, bubbles rise, planes and raindrops point along their path. Items: Max Items (scales all amounts down), Object Size, Depth Spread, Depth Haze (distant items fade), Color Variation, Variation Color. Themes, each with Amount and Color per item: Autumn (Leaf, Maple Seed, Chestnut, Twig, Feather), Street (Bowler, Cap, Paper Plane, Newspaper), Party (Confetti, Bubble, Heart, Note), Sky (Raindrop, Snowflake, Star, Star Twinkle). An Amount is a spawn maximum: items in flight stay until they leave the frame.",
			"displayName": "Autumn Wind",
			"identifier": "5c5509b5-6d07-4616-82b0-ba3475bcf9fe",
			"licenseName": "",
			"mail": "S.Mazur@cati-co.de",
